WEBVTT

00:37.280 --> 00:38.280
It's Her Majesty.

00:38.360 --> 00:39.720
Move aside!

00:40.320 --> 00:42.120
-Your Majesty!
-Please!

00:42.640 --> 00:43.720
You want to be killed?!

01:10.120 --> 01:12.200
Did you see the state of those fools?

01:12.280 --> 01:14.920
After all, they are only lowly plebs!

01:15.000 --> 01:17.360
All thanks to Her Majesty
for traveling to the frontlines

01:17.440 --> 01:20.120
and rallying the morale of our troops.

01:20.200 --> 01:21.400
Indeed!

01:21.480 --> 01:23.000
This is cause for celebration!

01:23.760 --> 01:25.400
How can you say that?!

01:25.480 --> 01:27.440
The subjects of the Kingdom
are starving even now!

01:28.800 --> 01:29.840
And so what?

01:29.920 --> 01:33.160
Are you suggesting we shouldn't reward
our soldiers for a battle well fought?

01:33.240 --> 01:37.080
Or do you have something against
celebrating the glory of our Queen?

01:37.160 --> 01:38.200
No, but...!

01:39.440 --> 01:43.120
Are you calling the outcome
of this skirmish to be a victory?!

01:43.200 --> 01:47.160
Until every last one of
those Imperial brutes are crushed,

01:47.240 --> 01:49.240
there will be no victory for our Kingdom.

01:51.000 --> 01:54.080
Y-yes, that's absolutely right,
Your Majesty!

01:54.160 --> 01:57.840
Of course! When I said "victory",
I didn't actually mean...

01:57.920 --> 02:00.760
Your Majesty,
what shall we do with these people?

02:03.120 --> 02:04.400
Ah, right, them.

02:06.200 --> 02:09.960
I've heard talk that their meddling
changed the tide of battle in our favor.

02:10.880 --> 02:11.880
Yes.

02:11.960 --> 02:14.760
They're an eccentric bunch,
both in speech and appearance.

02:15.640 --> 02:17.640
They're locked up
in the great prison for now.

02:17.720 --> 02:20.880
Forget about them.
We have no time for trivial matters.

02:20.960 --> 02:22.720
With all due respect, Your Majesty.

02:22.800 --> 02:25.760
I believe we can
put their weapons to good use.

02:25.840 --> 02:28.640
-It would make future battles...
-That's coward's talk!

02:29.480 --> 02:32.400
Are you not the hero
who once saved the Kingdom?

02:33.160 --> 02:37.440
The mighty knight who was blessed with
the sacred armor by the princess herself?

02:40.800 --> 02:42.920
I order you all
that by tomorrow's cabinet meeting,

02:43.000 --> 02:45.120
you prepare plans for the next battle.

02:45.760 --> 02:47.120
That is all.

02:49.120 --> 02:51.480
Excuse me, Mother.

02:52.880 --> 02:54.480
What is it, Fione?

02:55.200 --> 02:58.440
Well... it's about the strange people
that Cecil mentioned.

02:58.520 --> 03:01.760
-They might be the Empire's...
-I said to forget about them.

03:01.840 --> 03:04.480
Unless you have
reliable information to share?

03:05.920 --> 03:07.000
No.

03:07.520 --> 03:09.000
Then keep quiet.

03:35.840 --> 03:36.840
Come in.

03:37.680 --> 03:38.880
Greetings, Princess.

03:39.920 --> 03:40.920
You asked to see me?

03:42.840 --> 03:44.600
You're still not eating?

03:45.800 --> 03:49.000
Princess, skipping your meals
doesn't feed our people.

03:50.080 --> 03:51.720
I have no appetite.

03:53.240 --> 03:54.600
-Cecil?
-Yes?

03:55.480 --> 03:57.200
I have a favor to ask.

05:29.040 --> 05:30.880
Harleen Quinzel.

05:30.960 --> 05:33.320
A former psychiatrist at Arkham Asylum.

05:34.040 --> 05:36.720
Fell in love with the Joker
during his imprisonment there,

05:36.800 --> 05:38.760
then helped him escape.

05:38.840 --> 05:42.320
You've been partners in crime with him
ever since then, huh?

05:42.400 --> 05:44.760
A pretty dumb woman for a doctor.

05:44.840 --> 05:48.120
Fancied yourself a heroine
of a rom-com or what?

05:50.400 --> 05:53.280
How about you guys,
did you fail the officer exam?

05:54.440 --> 05:57.840
Prison guards are just muscle-heads
who couldn't hack it as cops.

05:57.920 --> 05:59.440
That's what I heard on TV.

06:00.840 --> 06:01.840
Stupid bitch!

06:05.280 --> 06:08.840
-Wake up!
-Quit lazing around get up!

06:08.920 --> 06:10.960
We're going to teach you a lesson...

06:14.560 --> 06:16.720
Rise and shine, Harley.

06:17.640 --> 06:18.640
Puddin'!

06:29.520 --> 06:31.080
Finally awake, eh, lady?

06:32.440 --> 06:33.800
Reality freaking bites.

06:35.000 --> 06:36.280
Oh, nothing!

06:38.240 --> 06:40.200
Do you guys realize what's going on?

06:41.400 --> 06:43.760
We've waited this long
and no one has come to get us,

06:43.840 --> 06:46.640
I guess that means
we aren't welcome around here.

06:46.720 --> 06:48.960
No shit, Sherlock!
Look around you!

06:50.920 --> 06:53.600
Anyone can see that
we're stuck in a goddamn prison!

06:54.120 --> 06:55.960
There's no need to shout.

06:56.040 --> 06:57.760
I'm just as frustrated as you.

06:58.400 --> 07:01.080
That battle was won due to our efforts.

07:01.160 --> 07:03.600
By all rights, they should
treat us as heroes,

07:03.680 --> 07:07.000
and call upon us for greater things,
like altering the fate of the Kingdom!

07:07.880 --> 07:08.880
Good grief.

07:08.960 --> 07:12.280
<i>I was on board with the idea of</i>
<i>being summoned to an Isekai.</i>

07:12.360 --> 07:14.720
But the God behind this whole thing

07:14.800 --> 07:16.880
seems to have no idea
how a story should work.

07:17.640 --> 07:19.480
I'll have to revise it myself.

07:19.560 --> 07:21.080
Now I get it.

07:21.160 --> 07:26.120
You're one of those annoying movie stars
who keeps forcing script changes, huh?

07:26.200 --> 07:28.320
No wonder I don't know you!

07:28.400 --> 07:30.000
You're a third-rate nobody!

07:30.080 --> 07:31.800
What did you just say?!

07:31.880 --> 07:33.160
Time is our problem.

07:34.920 --> 07:38.360
Three, two, one...

07:38.440 --> 07:43.080
And that marks exactly 12 hours
since the helicopter we were in crashed.

07:44.000 --> 07:46.800
If everything
that Amanda lady said is true,

07:47.440 --> 07:49.200
then after 72 hours...

07:49.280 --> 07:53.160
actually, in just 60 hours,
our heads will explode.

07:53.240 --> 07:55.720
We should return
to the helicopter by then.

07:57.120 --> 07:58.120
What?

07:58.200 --> 08:02.600
Holy crap. You actually have a brain
in that head of yours.

08:02.680 --> 08:05.360
Hold up, why are you
prioritizing the bombs?

08:05.440 --> 08:06.720
Don't you work for that hag?

08:06.800 --> 08:10.880
-What about your noble mission?
-The only lady I serve is liberty.

08:10.960 --> 08:13.760
I'm willing to do
what Amanda wants, if need be.

08:16.360 --> 08:18.440
I'm not happy with the way
the story is unfolding,

08:18.520 --> 08:21.600
but I don't see a reason
for us to stay here, either.

08:23.720 --> 08:25.520
We already kicked the hell outta the bars.

08:25.600 --> 08:27.440
Even the macho here couldn't do it.

08:27.520 --> 08:30.480
-There's no way you...
-Brute force isn't my style.

08:33.360 --> 08:36.920
Just hang tight.
I'll kick this story into gear.

08:38.560 --> 08:41.440
-But please bear one thing in mind.
-Huh?

08:41.520 --> 08:45.120
The hero woefully being forced
to leave his comrades behind

08:45.200 --> 08:48.480
and growing stronger from their sacrifice
is a common movie trope.

08:49.840 --> 08:52.080
Most of the time, the lady survives.

08:52.160 --> 08:56.200
Also typical is the another world hero
being asked to help the local princess.

08:56.280 --> 08:58.520
And ultimately falling in love with...

08:58.600 --> 09:00.800
-Guards!
-We got a prison break over here!

09:00.880 --> 09:02.560
Fools... Fools!

09:03.600 --> 09:05.840
You'll come in handy in the mission.

09:05.920 --> 09:07.080
I'm not letting you go!

09:21.400 --> 09:22.480
My powers...!

09:24.040 --> 09:28.000
-Hah! Sucks for you, buddy!
-Can't cause any trouble now.

09:28.520 --> 09:31.080
There's such a thing as narrative flow,
you know!

09:31.160 --> 09:33.760
What side character
gets in the way of the protagonist?!

09:34.280 --> 09:35.440
Screw you!

09:36.680 --> 09:37.840
<i>Get out.</i>

09:39.840 --> 09:43.000
-What the hell is this?
-Looks like soup.

09:43.080 --> 09:44.080
Probably.

09:49.080 --> 09:52.320
So, you're going to take us with you
this time, right?

09:52.400 --> 09:53.440
-No can do.
-What?

09:53.520 --> 09:55.080
It's these handcuffs.

09:55.160 --> 09:57.600
I haven't been able to use my powers
since these were put on.

09:57.680 --> 09:59.200
Why get in my way in the first place?!

09:59.280 --> 10:00.440
<i>-Hey.</i>
<i>-Huh?</i>

10:00.520 --> 10:02.600
<i>You're sitting in my seat.</i>

10:02.680 --> 10:06.520
<i>Don't get your human stench on it.</i>
<i>You'll infect me with your weakness.</i>

10:06.600 --> 10:10.760
<i>The stupid humans who came here</i>
<i>before you did the same damn thing.</i>

10:12.360 --> 10:15.280
-Say what?
-Come on, you must get the gist of it.

10:15.360 --> 10:18.880
The social rules of prison
are the same even in different worlds.

10:18.960 --> 10:20.080
-Hold on.
-Huh?

10:20.160 --> 10:22.640
Making a scene when we're short on time
isn't a smart move.

10:23.160 --> 10:25.680
Stuff it, Mr. Hide-My-Superpowers.

10:25.760 --> 10:27.640
We're different species
with different languages.

10:27.720 --> 10:30.760
We don't even share tastes in music,
and you expect me to get along with them?

10:30.840 --> 10:32.520
Remember what I showed you earlier?

10:32.600 --> 10:35.760
You and I are different, too.
Yet we can hold a conversation.

10:36.480 --> 10:38.160
-Isn't that right?
-Tsk.

10:38.240 --> 10:42.120
We really should've dragged that
other meta-human along with us.

10:42.720 --> 10:46.800
A reconciliation thanks to him
would be typical for a movie plot.

10:46.880 --> 10:48.360
Well, it can't be helped!

10:49.120 --> 10:51.720
We couldn't wake him up.
Probably too full or something.

10:51.800 --> 10:54.040
<i>Have you made a decision yet?</i>

10:54.120 --> 10:56.480
<i>That's my seat you're in.</i>

10:56.560 --> 10:58.360
Ah, my apologies.

10:58.440 --> 10:59.800
We're new around here.

10:59.880 --> 11:01.640
<i>What?</i>

11:01.720 --> 11:03.360
<i>Just get lost, already.</i>

11:03.440 --> 11:06.480
Of course.
We should've paid our respects first.

11:06.560 --> 11:10.200
You must be the boss here.
Everyone's attention is focused on you.

11:10.280 --> 11:11.920
It's quite impressive, really!

11:13.080 --> 11:14.320
You understand them?

11:14.400 --> 11:16.480
I'm reading the room
from their expressions and attitudes.

11:16.560 --> 11:18.160
A basic skill for an actor.

11:18.240 --> 11:21.000
Would you be so kind as to tell us
the rules around here?

11:21.520 --> 11:23.880
<i>What are you smiling about?</i>
<i>Are you screwing with me?</i>

11:23.960 --> 11:26.840
Indeed! The guards here
are downright deplorable.

11:26.920 --> 11:30.160
They like to pretend they have superiority
by beating us up.

11:30.240 --> 11:31.640
It's so pathetic!

11:31.720 --> 11:32.760
<i>I see how it is.</i>

11:32.840 --> 11:37.080
<i>The puny human thinks</i>
<i>he can mess with an ogre, eh?</i>

11:37.160 --> 11:38.280
Now then, let's...

11:53.920 --> 11:56.480
Freaking baaaaaarf!

12:17.000 --> 12:18.000
Ya like that?!

12:21.720 --> 12:22.720
Dumbass!

12:35.720 --> 12:37.000
<i>The wands! Bring the wands!</i>

12:37.080 --> 12:38.440
<i>Oh crap! Not the wands!</i>

12:38.520 --> 12:39.520
<i>Run!</i>

12:51.560 --> 12:54.200
<i>Throw them in the disciplinary cells!</i>
<i>All of them!</i>

12:56.920 --> 12:58.000
Hands off!

13:07.520 --> 13:08.760
What the hell was that!?

13:08.840 --> 13:10.800
Must've pulled some hocus pocus on us.

13:10.880 --> 13:14.080
<i>He said that shit was possible</i>
<i>in this "Isekai"  or whatever, right?</i>

13:18.840 --> 13:21.160
-Any luck?
-Who are you?

13:22.240 --> 13:25.840
You speak my language.
Did you come here from the other world?

13:25.920 --> 13:27.480
Why not introduce yourself first?

13:29.240 --> 13:30.600
Rick Flag.

13:31.160 --> 13:32.840
I'm an agent with A.R.G.U.S.

13:36.480 --> 13:37.880
"A.R.G.U.S.", huh?

13:37.960 --> 13:42.360
Let me guess. You must be buddies
with that old hag, Amanda, right?

13:43.760 --> 13:45.320
You must be Harley Quinn.

13:46.080 --> 13:49.960
Partner of the infamous Joker,
Gotham City's Clown Prince of Crime.

13:50.600 --> 13:54.040
Heh. So you know about me and Puddin'?

13:54.120 --> 13:55.400
Hot damn. You're her?

13:55.480 --> 14:02.360
Along with... Deadshot, Clayface,
Peacemaker, and King Shark.

14:03.080 --> 14:05.000
Yeah, well, what's your deal?

14:05.080 --> 14:08.680
By the looks of it, you've been here
way longer than us, yeah?

14:08.760 --> 14:10.880
When exactly did you all get here?

14:10.960 --> 14:12.520
Literally just yesterday.

14:12.600 --> 14:14.880
They fed us a bunch of nonsense,
and then boom.

14:16.840 --> 14:19.320
So Director Waller decided to send backup?

14:20.000 --> 14:22.760
No.
So she decided to get serious.

14:24.480 --> 14:27.200
Seems like you guys weren't
filled in on the details.

14:27.280 --> 14:30.760
You're not the first group
who got sent to this world.

14:30.840 --> 14:32.040
What does that mean?

14:32.720 --> 14:36.760
A few months ago, I led the squad
that was tasked with making first contact.

14:37.720 --> 14:39.400
With this strange world

14:40.040 --> 14:41.800
that's connected to ours through the Gate.

14:41.880 --> 14:45.400
<i>-So we are in an Isekai!  I knew it!</i>
<i>-But what for?</i>

14:46.960 --> 14:50.080
We're willing to go anywhere
to find water and natural resources.

14:50.160 --> 14:53.840
Monopolizing them would bring
immeasurable benefits to our country.

14:53.920 --> 14:57.360
It's even worth the risk of
exploring totally unknown worlds,

14:57.440 --> 14:59.640
that we might not return safely from.

14:59.720 --> 15:01.960
So, basically, you guys screwed up.

15:02.040 --> 15:03.760
And we're here to clean up the mess.

15:07.840 --> 15:10.600
We're a group of criminals.
Nobody gives a shit if we die.

15:11.280 --> 15:13.600
Some kinda "suicide squad", huh?

15:14.800 --> 15:16.880
Who was in charge of
leading your team here?

15:16.960 --> 15:19.440
If they had to replace me,
it must be Katana?

15:19.520 --> 15:20.880
Nope.

15:20.960 --> 15:23.920
It was somebody named
Adam or Eve or whatever.

15:24.000 --> 15:26.400
But he got squashed
when our helicopter crashed.

15:28.120 --> 15:29.560
The bomb in your necks?

15:29.640 --> 15:31.240
You've been briefed on that?

15:31.320 --> 15:34.600
We have exactly 58 hours,
29 minutes and 21 seconds left.

15:35.240 --> 15:37.320
We need to reset the timer.

15:37.400 --> 15:38.720
Where's the device?

15:38.800 --> 15:41.520
Timer? Reset?
What are you talking about?

15:41.600 --> 15:42.640
Don't play dumb!

15:42.720 --> 15:44.920
If you get in the way of my mission...!

15:46.160 --> 15:48.760
A time bomb?
Director Waller thought this through.

15:48.840 --> 15:50.520
You seriously don't know?

15:50.600 --> 15:52.440
Apparently, it receives radio signals.

15:53.320 --> 15:55.440
We share a common goal.

15:55.520 --> 15:56.560
I'll help you escape.

15:57.080 --> 15:59.480
Just to be clear, I have nothing on me.

15:59.560 --> 16:01.520
The device would have been
on your helicopter.

16:01.600 --> 16:03.160
All squished! Flat as a pancake!

16:04.120 --> 16:06.160
The signal must come
from beyond the Gate.

16:06.880 --> 16:11.160
To pick up radio waves from our world
we need to get it near the Gate.

16:11.240 --> 16:14.520
I should be able to guide you there,
if we came from the same entry point.

16:16.440 --> 16:18.440
So we're supposed to be
buddy-buddy now?

16:18.520 --> 16:21.520
After you assholes planted bombs in us
and just dumped us here?

16:21.600 --> 16:25.040
Would you prefer kicking the bucket
in 58 hours?

16:25.120 --> 16:27.560
You're just desperate to get out of here!

16:27.640 --> 16:31.400
It's easy to see that you're not used to
prison life like we are.

16:36.560 --> 16:38.280
Me hungry.

16:40.600 --> 16:42.120
Smell blood.

16:42.200 --> 16:43.400
W-w-w-wait a sec!

16:43.480 --> 16:44.640
You got to be kidding me.

16:44.720 --> 16:47.480
Aren't you friends?
How did you handle him before?!

16:47.560 --> 16:50.680
Don't ask me!
They brought us all here out of the blue!

16:52.160 --> 16:53.600
Hold on!

16:53.680 --> 16:55.280
Nanaue! Just wait!

16:55.960 --> 16:56.960
"Nanaue"?

16:57.040 --> 16:58.600
It's his real name.

16:58.680 --> 17:01.000
Nanaue, are you hungry?

17:01.080 --> 17:02.240
Well, so are we!

17:02.920 --> 17:05.880
There's food on the other side.
We can go together.

17:06.800 --> 17:10.600
-Other side?
-That's right. Come on, let's go.

17:19.000 --> 17:21.800
What's the matter?
The door should be unlocked.

17:23.400 --> 17:25.680
Come on, hurry up! Let's eat!

17:26.760 --> 17:27.880
<i>What are you doing?!</i>

17:27.960 --> 17:29.200
Make it quick, Nana!

17:36.760 --> 17:38.280
Take this!

17:42.280 --> 17:43.880
What just happened? Freaky.

17:47.720 --> 17:48.720
Holy crap.

17:51.400 --> 17:53.960
Let's go before the commotion
gets any bigger.

17:54.040 --> 17:55.480
Wrong! Make it bigger!

17:56.000 --> 17:57.200
You're out of your mind?

18:00.080 --> 18:01.080
Alright!

18:01.160 --> 18:02.480
Let me handle this.

18:12.720 --> 18:13.960
And the grand finale!

18:19.520 --> 18:21.200
I knew it! My powers are greater here!

18:24.120 --> 18:25.640
Listen closely, folks!

18:26.760 --> 18:29.680
The moment the power of true acting
surpassed language barriers...

18:29.760 --> 18:31.160
What are you dipshits waiting for?!

18:31.240 --> 18:32.760
-Huh?!
-The time is now!

18:32.840 --> 18:34.400
Did they neuter you or what?!

18:34.480 --> 18:35.720
Don't you have fangs and claws?!

18:35.800 --> 18:39.240
What the hell happened
to your fighting spirit?!

18:42.160 --> 18:43.520
Now's our chance!

19:56.840 --> 19:58.160
<i>Un,  deux,  trois!</i>

19:58.240 --> 20:00.640
<i>Un,  deux,  trois! Un,  deux,  trois!</i>

20:22.560 --> 20:25.120
<i>Could we talk to that girl</i>
<i>and her group?</i>

20:25.200 --> 20:26.200
What girl?

20:26.760 --> 20:27.880
Who do you mean?

20:27.960 --> 20:30.880
Those strange people
who appeared on the plains.

20:31.400 --> 20:33.400
According to your report,

20:33.480 --> 20:36.880
they were powerful enough
to turn the tide of battle, weren't they?

20:36.960 --> 20:39.200
Yes, that's true.

20:39.280 --> 20:41.160
Yet, we know nothing about
who or what they are.

20:41.240 --> 20:42.720
At the cabinet meeting,

20:42.800 --> 20:45.480
you spoke of them like
they had some kind of potential.

20:45.560 --> 20:48.400
I was merely interested
in their weaponry.

20:48.480 --> 20:50.880
I assigned one of our technicians
to take a closer look,

20:50.960 --> 20:52.920
but he's been totally baffled by them.

20:53.600 --> 20:56.520
War is about using
whatever resources we can, Princess.

20:56.600 --> 20:58.560
Please, Cecil.

20:59.080 --> 21:02.160
I wish to help in my own way.

21:02.240 --> 21:05.680
So that we can end the fighting
as quickly as possible.

21:07.560 --> 21:08.560
Sir Cecil!

21:09.960 --> 21:11.120
Look at that!

21:14.720 --> 21:15.720
What?!

21:22.360 --> 21:23.360
Oh?

21:24.480 --> 21:25.920
Looks like we've got company!

21:26.000 --> 21:29.600
Although they're going to need
way more troops to bring us down.

21:33.120 --> 21:34.720
Frigging idiots...

21:34.800 --> 21:38.680
You don't have time be wasting
on this shit!

23:03.000 --> 23:06.000
Subtitles: Radha Shiotani Case
plint.com
